    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §361-b, Exec L (as proposed in S.5991 & A.7594)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7188\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to reports by the women\nveterans coordinator\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2019,\nc.480.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding a technical\nqualifier regarding the reports required on topics including, but not\nlimited to, the demographics of women veterans, the number of women\nveterans listed by county, and the unique needs of the women veterans\npopulation. The amendment provides that the reports will contain such\ninformation \"to the extent such information is available.\"\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 16 of 2019, the Executive noted that this\ntechnical amendment will ensure that New York State's Women Veterans\nCoordinator can continue to comply with her statutory duties by clarify-\ning that the reports required by this legislation are to be completed to\nthe extent such information necessary is available to the Coordinator.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 480 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2019 amending the executive law relating to the\nwomen veterans coordinator, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\n5.5991 and A.7594, takes effect.\n",
